   "id": "kospi-chip-rout-3-nov",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Seoul stocks slide 3.6% as Samsung and SK hynix lead a chip sell-off",
   "when": "Tue 3 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "The KOSPI closed at 5,648.79, down 3.59%. Samsung Electronics lost 4.15% and SK hynix 5.03%. Foreign investors sold a net 1.5 trillion won of shares, while individual investors bought 1.7 trillion won. Decliners beat gainers by 656 to 220. Local reports blame doubts that heavy AI spending will pay off, after the US chip index fell 3.4% on Monday. The won was around 1,341 per dollar.",
   "why": "Korea is about 18% of your portfolio, mostly through SCBKEQTG, and chips dominate the index. This morning your dashboard prices SCBKEQTG at its 29 Oct NAV. The KOSPI had already fallen about 1.3% by 2 Nov and fell again on 3 Nov, so the fund's real value is lower than shown. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive.",
   "dir": "neg",
