   "id": "wall-street-chip-rebound-3-nov",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "US stocks edge up on a chip rebound as the midterm vote runs",
   "when": "Tue 3 Nov · US close",
   "what": "The S&P 500 rose 0.36% to 7,568.92, ending a three-day losing run. The Nasdaq Composite gained 0.83% to 25,372.01. The Dow slipped 0.38%, held back by Apple. AMD and Broadcom rose about 3%, and Micron and Nvidia more than 2%. The Nasdaq-100 is still about 10% below its recent high. The 10-year Treasury yield ended near 4.95%, up 6 basis points on our market data. Counting of midterm votes was starting.",
   "why": "The US is about 25% of your portfolio, mostly funds tracking the S&P 500. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at 29 Oct NAVs, and the S&P 500 is down about 2% since then. The dashboard refreshes at 11:30. A rebound after Monday's chip losses helps, but the Korean sell-off shows the AI-spending doubt is still active.",
