   "headline": "Apple posts record-high revenue, but a soft margin outlook trims its shares",
   "when": "Mon 2 Nov · after US close",
   "what": "Apple reported fiscal fourth-quarter revenue of $114.5 billion, up 12%, and diluted earnings of $2.10 a share, up 14%. Earnings include a $0.05 benefit from tariff refunds. Its quarterly dividend is $0.27 a share, payable 16 Nov to holders on record at 12 Nov. CNBC says the shares fell almost 2% on Tuesday after a weak margin forecast, and iPad sales missed estimates.",
