   "id": "binance-theft-crypto-outflows",
   "group": "Crypto",
   "headline": "Binance theft fallout and ETF outflows keep crypto cautious",
   "when": "Tue 3 Nov",
   "what": "About $6.3 billion left Binance on 29 Oct in roughly 20 minutes. The FBI linked it to North Korea on 31 Oct. On Tuesday Kim Yo-jong rejected that finding. Binance customers have withdrawn a net $4.72 billion since the exchange reopened on Sunday. US spot bitcoin ETFs lost $399 million on Monday, their second day of outflows. Bitcoin dipped to about $76,300 and later traded near $76,900.",
   "why": "Crypto is about 5.7% of your portfolio. BNB is the token of the exchange at the centre of the theft, and Bitcoin and Ether are caught in the wider caution. Fund outflows and the election add to the pressure. Our market tile shows bitcoin at $77,700, up 1.32% over 24 hours.",
